{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:product-metric","title":"def:product-metric","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":447,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:product-metric","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:product-form-positive-definite]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:smooth-tensor-field-add]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-immersion-metric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:product-metric","line":744,"source":"\\begin{definition}[The Product Metric]\n\\label{def:product-metric}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-metric, lem:product-form-positive-definite, lem:smooth-tensor-field-add, lem:pullback-immersion-metric}\n\n\n\n\nFor Riemannian manifolds $(M_1,g_1)$ and $(M_2,g_2)$, the \\emph{product metric} on $M_1\\times M_2$ is the metric (2.12). It is symmetric, positive definite by Lemma \\ref{lem:product-form-positive-definite}, and smooth by (2.12') and Lemma \\ref{lem:smooth-tensor-field-add}, since each pullback summand is smooth.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[The Product Metric] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a70726f647563742d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aproduct-form-positive-definite\">↗ lem:product-form-positive-definite</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asmooth-tensor-field-add\">↗ lem:smooth-tensor-field-add</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apullback-immersion-metric\">↗ lem:pullback-immersion-metric</a> <p></p>For Riemannian manifolds <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M_1,g_1)$\">$(M_1,g_1)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M_2,g_2)$\">$(M_2,g_2)$</span>, the <em>product metric</em> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M_1\\times M_2$\">$M_1\\times M_2$</span> is the metric (2.12). It is symmetric, positive definite by Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aproduct-form-positive-definite\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:product-form-positive-definite\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a70726f647563742d666f726d2d706f7369746976652d646566696e697465\">2</a>, and smooth by (2.12&#x27;) and Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Asmooth-tensor-field-add\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:smooth-tensor-field-add\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a736d6f6f74682d74656e736f722d6669656c642d616464\">2</a>, since each pullback summand is smooth. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:product-form-positive-definite","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:product-metric-torus","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id"