ersion-metric}\n\n\n\n\nFor Riemannian manifolds $(M_1,g_1)$ and $(M_2,g_2)$, the \\emph{product metric} on $M_1\\times M_2$ is the metric (2.12). It is symmetric, positive definite by Lemma \\ref{lem:product-form-positive-definite}, and smooth by (2.12') and Lemma \\ref{lem:smooth-tensor-field-add}, since each pullback summand is smooth.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:product-form-positive-definite","title":"lem:product-form-positive-definite","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:smooth-tensor-field-add","title":"lem:smooth-tensor-field-add","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-immersion-metric","title":"lem:pullback-immersion-metric","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}